window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Bella Rose Braxton wasn't supposed to be a beta.</b></p> <p>After her sweet sixteen ends in disaster, Rosie thinks life can't get any worse. Returning to school after the party, she realizes how far a beta can fall. It doesn't take her long to see that playing by the rules never did her any favors, and she vows to take the first exit out of Knotty Pines.</p> <p>But circumstances get in the way, and more than ten years later, she's still in her hometown. Despite what happened in high school, she thought she had moved on and made a nice, quiet life for herself.</p> <p>Then, Dane freaking Daniels walks back into town. He's a former college football star turned winning coach and the one alpha Rosie never wants to see again.</p> <p>And who is with him?</p> <p>Nash Wells, the other alpha at the top of her hide-from-them-in-public list.</p> <p>She thought she could ignore Pack Daniels like she does the rest of her hometown. That was before the two alphas and their handsome omega moved in next door.</p> <p>Her new neighbors will stop at nothing to prove to Rosie that she's meant to be theirs. But how can Rosie trust such an unlikely match? Can Dane, Nash, and Quinn convince Rosie to let go of the past so they can have a future?</p> <p>Unlikely <i>is a small-town why-choose romance that includes football, nosy neighbors, found family, a curvy beta FMC, and a male omega.</i></p>"; 
